      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Eq 8.5, upper scheme, alpha-alpha channel (arrow labelled 'aa'). Radical-driven McLafferty rearrangement of the hexanal molecular ion: the O-centred odd electron abstracts the gamma-H, the resulting C-radical drives Ca-Cb cleavage, and the C2H4O enol fragment retains BOTH charge and radical (IE(enol)=9.2 eV printed right of the dashed line; lowest IE -> base peak). Book draws 4 fishhook arcs (O gamma-H abstraction; Cb=Cg pi formation; Ca-Cb cleavage); moves 1,4,6 correspond to those drawn arcs, moves 2,3,5 are the implicit partner homolysis/pairing hooks required for electron balance (not drawn). Product written as the distonic enol radical cation .CH2-CH=O(+)H; the page draws the resonance form HO-CH=CH2 with +. shown on oxygen. m/z curator-computed; 100% printed. [RECHECK 2026-07-24: arc count corrected 3->4 per a zoomed re-read; the gamma-H abstraction is drawn as TWO barbs (O-radical->H and the gamma C-H bond electron->O-H), not one.]"
    },
