      "confidence": 0.4,
      "curator_note": "Cross-link: M\u00d8D rule IMS_8_5_1. Same caveat as the alpha-i record: the rule's skeleton (gamma-H -> O, Ca-Cb cleavage, Cb=Cg + enol C=C) matches this hexanal McLafferty, but the rule is over-valent (carbonyl C valence 5, extra H, reactant C6H13O) and non-conserving (products +2 / 2 radicals vs +1/1), so it is chemically invalid as written and guardrail-dropped. IMS_8_5_1 localizes the charge on the butene, i.e. the alpha-i (not this alpha-alpha) outcome."
